@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il34-nouns`

-- National Insurance Law s 336 (the payment period), s 340 (work-injury and maternity contribution rates), s 340A (a household worker) and s 343 (reduced
-- contributions for an approved employer). Row IL-34, priority 5. `src:N` is line N of the Law's deposited text
-- (../../registers/source-bundle/national-insurance-law-consolidated-version-5755-1995.he.wiki.txt, sha256 78bf47ee...2a97).
--
-- WHERE THE TEXT AND THE TEMPORARY FIGURES MEET. Ss 340(d) and (e) and 340A were added from 1 January 2025 by the National Insurance Law (Amendment No. 252 and
-- temporary provision), Sefer HaChukim 3347 p. 176 (../../registers/source-bundle/amending-laws/25_lsr_5482787.pdf, sha256 d6c450ca...8904). The consolidation prints
-- the base figure in the text (0.4%, 0.1%, 6.25%, 1%, 2%) and the figure of 2025 and 2026 in an editors' note (0.53%, 0.13%, 7.85%, 1.8%, 3.6%). That Act's s 7(a)
-- says why: for contributions collected for 2025 and 2026 the Law is read with the larger figures, from the commencement day to 21 Tevet 5787 (31 December 2026);
-- and s 7(b) lets the Minister of Finance extend the temporary period, by order, to 2027 and then 2028, a year at a time. So the figure turns on the YEAR, and on
-- whether an order extended it for 2027 or 2028 (a fact the caller reports). Before 2025 these provisions did not exist.
--
-- Rates here are fractions (0.0053 is 0.53%). The average wage is an input.

§ `Sections 336, 340, 340A and 343`

§§ `Section 336: the payment period`

-- src:3622 | סעיף 336 – תחומה של תקופת תשלום
-- src:3623 | כל תקופת תשלום תסתיים בסופו של כל חודש, אם לא קבע השר תחומים אחרים לתקופת תשלום, בין לכל המבוטחים ובין לסוג מבוטחים.

-- "Every payment period shall end at the end of every month, if the Minister has not fixed other limits for a payment period, for all the insured or for a
-- class of the insured." No order setting other limits is deposited: if one applies, the caller says so, and the period is declined.
@ref National Insurance Law s 336 (source line 3623)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`an order of the Minister under section 336 sets other limits for this payment period, and it is not deposited` MEANS
    REFUSE "an order of the Minister under section 336 sets other limits for this payment period, and it is not deposited"

@ref National Insurance Law s 336 (source line 3623)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the Minister set other limits for the insured concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`s 336 — the last day of the payment period holding the day` d `, other limits having been set being` `the Minister set other limits for the insured concerned` MEANS
    IF `the Minister set other limits for the insured concerned`
    THEN `an order of the Minister under section 336 sets other limits for this payment period, and it is not deposited`
    ELSE YMD (DATE_YEAR d) (DATE_MONTH d) (`Days in month` (DATE_MONTH d) (DATE_YEAR d))

§§ `The temporary figures of 2025 and 2026 (Amendment No. 252 s 6 and s 7)`

@ref Amendment No. 252 s 6 (commencement 1 January 2025) and s 7(a)-(b)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`this provision was added by Amendment No. 252 from 1 January 2025 and did not exist before` MEANS
    REFUSE "this provision was added by Amendment No. 252 from 1 January 2025 and did not exist before"

-- Is the year within the temporary period: 2025 and 2026 by the Act itself; 2027 and 2028 only if the Minister of Finance extended it by order for that year.
@ref Amendment No. 252 s 7(a)-(b)
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the temporary period was extended for the year by order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the temporary figures apply in the year` `the year` `, an order extending the temporary period being` `the temporary period was extended for the year by order` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the year` LESS THAN 2025                                    THEN `this provision was added by Amendment No. 252 from 1 January 2025 and did not exist before`
           IF `the year` EQUALS 2025 OR `the year` EQUALS 2026            THEN TRUE
           IF `the year` EQUALS 2027 OR `the year` EQUALS 2028            THEN `the temporary period was extended for the year by order`
           OTHERWISE                                                            FALSE

§§ `Section 340: work-injury and maternity insurance`

-- src:3637 | סעיף 340 – דמי ביטוח נפגעי עבודה ואימהות [תיקון: תשנ״ח, תש״ס־2, תשס״ה־6, תשפ״ה־3]
-- src:3638 | (א) שיעורי דמי ביטוח בענף ביטוח נפגעי עבודה הם –
-- src:3639 | (1) לגבי מבוטח שהוא עובד או עובד עצמאי – כאמור בפרט 4 בלוח י׳ ובסעיף 337;
-- src:3640 | (2) לגבי מבוטח אחר – שיעורי דמי ביטוח שקבע השר, ובלבד שלא יעלו על השיעור האמור בפרט 4 בלוח י׳ ובסעיף 337.
-- src:3641 | (ב) השר רשאי לקבוע הוראות משלימות בדבר חישוב ההכנסה לענין סעיף זה.
-- src:3642 | (ג) שיעורי דמי ביטוח בענף ביטוח אימהות לגבי מי שמתגורר באזור ואינו תושב ישראל באזור, והכל כהגדרתם בסעיף 378, יהיו בשיעור של 70% מהשיעור האמור בפרט 1 בלוח י׳ ובסעיף 337.
-- src:3643 | (ד) על אף הוראות סעיף קטן (א)(2), לגבי מי שנמצא בהכשרה מקצועית או בשיקום מקצועי כאמור בסעיף 75(א)(3), ישולמו דמי ביטוח נפגעי עבודה בשיעור 0.4% [note: (בשנים 2025–2026: 0.53%)] ממחצית השכר הממוצע, על ידי מי שרואים אותו כמעסיקו של אותו אדם לפי סעיף 75(ב).
-- src:3644 | (ה) לגבי מי שמלאו לו 18 שנים ונמצא בהכשרה מקצועית כהגדרתה בסעיף 39, ישולמו דמי ביטוח אימהות בשיעור 0.1% [note: (בשנים 2025–2026: 0.13%)] ממחצית השכר הממוצע, על ידי מי שרואים אותו כמעסיקו של אותו אדם לפי סעיף 55.
-- src:3646 | סעיף 340א – דמי ביטוח לעובד במשק בית [תיקון: תשפ״ה־3]
-- src:3647 | (א)(1) על אף האמור בסעיפים 337 ו־340, דמי הביטוח שישלם מעסיק בעד עובד במשק בית המבוטח לפי פרק י״א, לתקופה של רבעון כהגדרתו בלוח י״א, יהיו בשיעור של 6.25% [note: (בשנים 2025–2026: 7.85%)] מהשכר שילם לו המעסיק באותה תקופת תשלום.
-- src:3648 | (2) מעסיק יהיה רשאי לנכות משכרו של עובד כאמור בפסקה (1), 1% [note: (בשנים 2025–2026: 1.8%)] מהשכר שבעדו הוא משלם לו דמי ביטוח לפי אותה פסקה.
-- src:3649 | (ב) על אף האמור בסעיף קטן (א), דמי הביטוח שישלם מעסיק לתקופת התשלום כאמור באותו סעיף קטן, בעד עובד במשק בית שאינו מבוטח לפי פרק י״א או שמתקיימות בו הוראות סעיף 351(ב) או (ד), יהיו 2% [note: (בשנים 2025–2026: 3.6%)] מהשכר ששילם לו המעסיק בעד אותה תקופת תשלום.
-- src:3650 | (ג) לעניין סעיף זה –
-- src:3651 | ”עובד במשק בית“ – מי שמועסק אצל יחיד שלא למטרת עסק או משלח יד;
-- src:3652 | ”שכר“ – הכנסה מהמקורות המפורטים בסעיף 2(2) לפקודת מס הכנסה.

-- (a)(2): for an insured person who is neither an employee nor self-employed, the Minister fixes the rate, not above the item 4 rate "and in s 337". Schedule J
-- prints no rate for that column in item 4 (a dash), so the ceiling is not a number.
@ref National Insurance Law s 340(a)(2) (source line 3640); Schedule J item 4 (source line 4723)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Schedule J item 4 prints no rate (a dash) for an insured person who is neither an employee nor self-employed, so the ceiling of section 340(a)(2) is not a number` MEANS
    REFUSE "Schedule J item 4 prints no rate (a dash) for an insured person who is neither an employee nor self-employed, so the ceiling of section 340(a)(2) is not a number"

@ref National Insurance Law s 340(a)(2) (source line 3640)
GIVEN `the rate the Minister fixed` IS A NUMBER
      `the item 4 rate for this column` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 340(a)(2) — the rate fixed for another insured person is valid: fixed` `the rate the Minister fixed` `, the item 4 rate` `the item 4 rate for this column` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the item 4 rate for this column`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `Schedule J item 4 prints no rate (a dash) for an insured person who is neither an employee nor self-employed, so the ceiling of section 340(a)(2) is not a number`
    WHEN JUST c  THEN `the rate the Minister fixed` AT MOST c

-- (c): maternity insurance for one who lives in the Area and is not an Israeli resident in the Area (both as s 378 defines): 70% of the item 1 rate.
@ref National Insurance Law s 340(c) (source line 3642)
GIVEN `the item 1 rate for this column` IS A NUMBER
      `lives in the Area and is not an Israeli resident in the Area, as section 378 defines` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 340(c) — the maternity insurance rate: item 1 rate` `the item 1 rate for this column` `, a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli resident there being` `lives in the Area and is not an Israeli resident in the Area, as section 378 defines` MEANS
    IF `lives in the Area and is not an Israeli resident in the Area, as section 378 defines`
    THEN 70% TIMES `the item 1 rate for this column`
    ELSE `the item 1 rate for this column`

-- (d): vocational training or rehabilitation under s 75(a)(3): work-injury contributions of 0.4% of half the average wage (2025 and 2026: 0.53%), paid by
-- whoever is regarded as his employer under s 75(b). (e): maternity insurance for one aged 18 or more in vocational training as s 39 defines it: 0.1% (0.13%) of half
-- the average wage, paid by whoever s 55 regards as his employer.
@ref National Insurance Law s 340(d) (source line 3643); Amendment No. 252 s 4, s 7(a)(1)(a)
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the temporary period was extended for the year by order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the average wage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 340(d) — the monthly work-injury contribution for training or rehabilitation, year` `the year` `, an order extending the temporary period being` `the temporary period was extended for the year by order` `, the average wage being` `the average wage` MEANS
    IF `the temporary figures apply in the year` `the year` `, an order extending the temporary period being` `the temporary period was extended for the year by order`
    THEN 0.53% TIMES (`the average wage` DIVIDED BY 2)
    ELSE 0.4% TIMES (`the average wage` DIVIDED BY 2)

@ref National Insurance Law s 340(e) (source line 3644); Amendment No. 252 s 4, s 7(a)(1)(b)
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the temporary period was extended for the year by order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the average wage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 340(e) — the monthly maternity contribution for vocational training, year` `the year` `, an order extending the temporary period being` `the temporary period was extended for the year by order` `, the average wage being` `the average wage` MEANS
    IF `the temporary figures apply in the year` `the year` `, an order extending the temporary period being` `the temporary period was extended for the year by order`
    THEN 0.13% TIMES (`the average wage` DIVIDED BY 2)
    ELSE 0.1% TIMES (`the average wage` DIVIDED BY 2)

§§ `Section 340A: an employee in a household`


-- An employer of a household worker (employed by an individual not for a business or profession) insured under Chapter 11, for a quarter as Schedule K defines it,
-- pays 6.25% (2025 and 2026: 7.85%) of the wage he paid in the quarter, and may deduct 1% (1.8%) of that wage from the worker's wage. If the worker is not insured
-- under Chapter 11, or s 351(b) or (d) applies to him, the employer pays 2% (3.6%).
@ref National Insurance Law s 340A(a)(1) and (b) (source lines 3647, 3649); Amendment No. 252 s 5, s 7(a)(2)
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the temporary period was extended for the year by order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the wage paid in the quarter` IS A NUMBER
      `the worker is insured under Chapter 11 and neither section 351(b) nor (d) applies to him` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 340A — the employer's contributions for a household worker for a quarter, year` `the year` `, an order extending the temporary period being` `the temporary period was extended for the year by order` `, wage` `the wage paid in the quarter` `, insured under Chapter 11 and not under section 351(b) or (d) being` `the worker is insured under Chapter 11 and neither section 351(b) nor (d) applies to him` MEANS
    `the wage paid in the quarter` TIMES `the rate`
    WHERE
        `the temporary` MEANS `the temporary figures apply in the year` `the year` `, an order extending the temporary period being` `the temporary period was extended for the year by order`
        `the rate` MEANS
            IF `the worker is insured under Chapter 11 and neither section 351(b) nor (d) applies to him`
            THEN (IF `the temporary` THEN 7.85% ELSE 6.25%)
            ELSE (IF `the temporary` THEN 3.6% ELSE 2%)

@ref National Insurance Law s 340A(a)(2) (source line 3648); Amendment No. 252 s 5, s 7(a)(2)
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the temporary period was extended for the year by order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the wage paid in the quarter` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 340A(a)(2) — the most the employer may deduct from the worker's wage for a quarter, year` `the year` `, an order extending the temporary period being` `the temporary period was extended for the year by order` `, wage` `the wage paid in the quarter` MEANS
    IF `the temporary figures apply in the year` `the year` `, an order extending the temporary period being` `the temporary period was extended for the year by order`
    THEN 1.8% TIMES `the wage paid in the quarter`
    ELSE 1% TIMES `the wage paid in the quarter`

§§ `Section 343: reduced contributions for an approved employer`

-- src:3677 | סעיף 343 – דמי ביטוח מופחתים
-- src:3678 | השר רשאי לקבוע כי מעביד שאישר לכך ישלם דמי ביטוח מופחתים לענין סעיף 340 כפי שיקבע, ובלבד שנתמלאו בו תנאים אלה:
-- src:3679 | (1) הוא מעביד לפחות חמש מאות עובדים;
-- src:3680 | (2) הוא חייב, בתוקף חוק, הסכם קיבוצי או חוזה עבודה, לשלם לעובדים שכר בעד הזמן שבעדו משתלמים דמי פגיעה בעבודה לפי סעיף 92, וסך כל השכר אינו קטן מדמי הפגיעה (להלן – תמורת דמי פגיעה).

@ref National Insurance Law s 343 (source line 3678)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the reduced contributions the Minister determined under section 343 are not in the sources` MEANS
    REFUSE "the reduced contributions the Minister determined under section 343 are not in the sources"

-- The Minister may determine that an employer he has approved pays reduced contributions, provided (1) he employs at least 500 employees and (2) he is bound by
-- law, a collective agreement or a contract of work to pay wages for the time injury allowance is paid under s 92, and the total wages are not less than the allowance.
@ref National Insurance Law s 343 (source lines 3679-3680)
GIVEN e IS AN `An employer's position under section 343`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 343 — the employer is one the Minister may approve` e MEANS
        e's `the number of employees` AT LEAST 500
    AND e's `bound by law, a collective agreement or a contract to pay wages for the time injury allowance is paid`
    AND e's `the total wages the employer pays for that time` AT LEAST e's `the injury allowance paid for that time`

@ref National Insurance Law s 343 (source line 3678)
GIVEN e IS AN `An employer's position under section 343`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 343 — the reduced contribution for an approved employer` e MEANS
    IF `s 343 — the employer is one the Minister may approve` e
    THEN `the reduced contributions the Minister determined under section 343 are not in the sources`
    ELSE REFUSE "the employer does not meet the conditions of section 343 and cannot be approved for reduced contributions"
